/T (Key findings)
/E (Key findings)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 77 0 R
/T (Recognising human rights and interests is not the same as ensuring they remain protected. Participants raised culture, relationships, autonomy and democratic life as interests worth preserving, but disagreed about what could protect them if humans lost economic leverage and could no longer enforce their claims. The discussion highlighted a central tension between recognising human value and ensuring that human interests remain protected when familiar sources of leverage weaken.)
/E (Recognising human rights and interests is not the same as ensuring they remain protected. Participants raised culture, relationships, autonomy and democratic life as interests worth preserving, but disagreed about what could protect them if humans lost economic leverage and could no longer enforce their claims. The discussion highlighted a central tension between recognising human value and ensuring that human interests remain protected when familiar sources of leverage weaken.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 77 0 R
/T (Losing control over large-scale systems does not necessarily mean losing autonomy in everyday life, however, people cannot assume their choices would remain protected. Some participants argued that local decision-making and human-AI co-agency could survive under particular conditions. Others questioned how secure those choices would be if a more powerful system could override them without consent or any way to challenge its actions. )
/E (Losing control over large-scale systems does not necessarily mean losing autonomy in everyday life, however, people cannot assume their choices would remain protected. Some participants argued that local decision-making and human-AI co-agency could survive under particular conditions. Others questioned how secure those choices would be if a more powerful system could override them without consent or any way to challenge its actions. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 77 0 R
/T (Humans and advanced AI systems might cooperate even if humans could no longer reliably control AI, but sustaining that cooperation would require credible commitments. Shared goals give both sides reasons to work together without requiring identical values, while incentives and ways to detect broken agreements might help sustain trust. The unresolved challenge was how either side would verify that commitments were honoured over time, and what options humans would have if a more capable system broke them. )
/E (Humans and advanced AI systems might cooperate even if humans could no longer reliably control AI, but sustaining that cooperation would require credible commitments. Shared goals give both sides reasons to work together without requiring identical values, while incentives and ways to detect broken agreements might help sustain trust. The unresolved challenge was how either side would verify that commitments were honoured over time, and what options humans would have if a more capable system broke them. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
