/P 79 0 R
/T (What post-control means)
/E (What post-control means)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (For this report, a post-control scenario is one in which advanced AI systems have become sufficiently capable, autonomous or embedded in important processes that humans can no longer reliably direct or constrain them in the ways they currently do. Such a scenario could also involve a substantial decline in the economic need for human labour and cognition, weakening forms of influence that have historically followed from participation in production, consumption and collective decision-making.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Loss of control does not necessarily occur at the same time as the loss of knowledge, bargaining power, political influence or personal autonomy. These changes may overlap, and understanding their relationship is important for identifying where human agency begins to weaken. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 79 0 R
/T (Two readings that open the question)
/E (Two readings that open the question)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Gradual Disempowerment, Kulveit and colleagues \(2025\). This research describes how incremental increases in AI capabilities could weaken human influence across the economy, culture and the state, including through the gradual replacement of labour and cognition and through feedback loops that make institutions less dependent on human participation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
