/P 84 0 R
/E (This argument suggests that local autonomy does not always depend on maintaining control over the entire system. However, it also raises a distinction between freedom that a more capable system happens to leave available and freedom that people have a recognised and protected right to exercise.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
