<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (These approaches can be explored through different methods to better understand how cooperation might work under unequal power. It might be useful to distinguish if an agreement continues to hold when incentives change, or whether violations can be detected, and what options humans would have if an agreement is broken. Examples of tests are:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 716 0 R
/E (Simulations and tabletop exercises can help examine how humans and AI systems negotiate and respond to changing incentives, while behavioural tests can assess how consistently AI systems honour agreements under different conditions. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 717 0 R
/E (Lessons from existing international agreements, such as nuclear non-proliferation, may also help identify what makes commitments credible, how compliance is monitored and how authority is shared among participants.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
