/K [4]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The approaches outlined above offer a starting point for identifying possible policy priorities, drawing on the roundtable discussions and the analysis presented in this report. Each requires further development, and additional approaches may emerge as our understanding of advanced AI evolves.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (For policymakers, a central challenge is determining who should act, what responsibilities they should hold and which mechanisms they can realistically implement. These decisions will also depend on the different capacities and sources of strategic leverage available to each jurisdiction. Some governments may have greater influence over frontier AI development, while others may need to adapt their governance arrangements or work through international coordination.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (By setting out possible measures alongside their unresolved challenges, the table highlights areas that require closer attention in policy design and implementation. Further work can examine how existing human institutions might use their influence today, and how the decisions they make could shape future post-control scenarios and the protection of human interests.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
