349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (This report has explored what might make human claims and cooperation meaningful if advanced AI systems move beyond reliable human control. The possible pathways towards declining human agency provided context for two roundtables examining the protection of human interests and the conditions for cooperation. Contributions from participants with diverse professional and disciplinary backgrounds enriched the analysis, bringing different perspectives and assumptions into the discussion without limiting it to a single hypothesis. The resulting findings address three interconnected issues concerning the protection of human claims, the possibilities and limits of local autonomy, and the reliability of cooperation.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Post-control scenarios could lead to very different futures. Advanced AI systems that support human interests might enable extraordinary improvements in prosperity and wellbeing, while systems pursuing incompatible objectives could lead to catastrophic harm. Even a future in which human material needs are fully met would leave important questions about autonomy and participation unresolved.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (This is what makes loss of control such a consequential risk. As human economic leverage weakens and more decisions are delegated to AI systems, societies may gradually lose the ability to scrutinise or challenge decisions that affect them. If advanced systems eventually pursue objectives that diverge from human interests, the institutions responsible for protecting those interests may no longer have effective means to intervene.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The discussions highlight the importance of examining post-control futures before they emerge. Understanding how human agency might weaken, the conditions that may help preserve it and the role of existing institutions can inform decisions while there is still an opportunity to shape AI development and governance. Ultimately, the challenge extends beyond ensuring that advanced AI produces beneficial outcomes to considering the role humans will have in shaping the future those systems help create.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
