<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (This report draws on two ninety-minute online roundtables held on 15 and 20 October 2026, as part of a four-session series convened by the Post-Control Initiative. The discussions brought together invited specialists from different academic and professional backgrounds and followed a structured format that encouraged participants to challenge assumptions, consider alternative perspectives and explore possible responses to post-control scenarios.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (The analysis brings together recurring themes, disagreements and underlying assumptions from both discussions, connecting them with relevant research. As an exploratory exercise, the roundtables were intended to open questions and examine different possibilities, not to establish consensus or provide definitive answers. The findings and possible policy priorities presented in this report are therefore an analytical synthesis, and contributions are reported without individual attribution.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (The broader Post-Control Initiative included two additional sessions held on 14 and 16 October 2026, exploring other questions within the initiative's wider scope.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
